  // 128x64, 1bpp, row-major, standard XBM bit order (bit N of byte = pixel
  // x = byteIndex*8+N within that row). bit=1 -> black, derived pixel-for-
  // pixel from the FoxFW wallpaper template. Identical layout to what
  // canvas_draw_xbm() in FoxFW2.0's desktop.c actually renders, and to the
  // default wallpaper.xbm the firmware auto-creates on first boot. This is
  // just the ARTWORK to render/bake into the locked band below â€” which
  // pixels are actually off-limits to the user is decided by isLocked(),
  // not by which of these bits happen to be black or white.
